## Context

PR #205 (ticket 0180) extended the unknown-flag rejection convention to
archive, migrate, next-id, validate, list. A celebrate sweep found three
remaining commands with the same class of defect:

- `ready.go` cmdReady: the switch has `case explicit == "":` before a
  `default:` error branch. An unknown `--flag` hits the `explicit == ""`
  arm and is silently stored as the directory path, producing a confusing
  `resolveDir` error instead of "unknown flag".
- `update.go` cmdUpdate: signature is `(_ []string)` — all args are
  silently discarded.
- `version.go` cmdVersion: same `(_ []string)` pattern — all args
  silently discarded.

## Relevant files

- `src/go/ready.go`   — fix the switch ordering so `-`-prefixed args
                        are checked before the `explicit == ""` fallthrough
- `src/go/update.go`  — add flag-reject loop; replace `_` with `args`
- `src/go/version.go` — add flag-reject loop; replace `_` with `args`
- `src/go/rm.go`      — reference implementation of the convention

## Actions

1. `ready.go`: add `case strings.HasPrefix(a, "-") && a != "--json":` arm
   before `case explicit == "":` so unknown flags error out.
2. `update.go`: change `_ []string` to `args []string`, add flag-reject
   loop at the top of cmdUpdate.
3. `version.go`: same as update.go.
4. Add unknown-flag shell integration tests to `tests/test_ready.sh`,
   `tests/test_update.sh`, `tests/test_version.sh`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All 3 commands reject unknown `-`-prefixed flags with non-zero exit
      and a "unknown flag" usage message
- [ ] Existing positional/flag behavior unchanged — `make check` passes
- [ ] Shell integration tests cover unknown-flag rejection for each command
